th("That one recipe, done carefully, will teach you more than any twelve-piece kit, because every step is one you did on purpose and can repeat.")
# ===== ACT 7 mistakes to avoid =====
th("Before you go, let me save you from the three mistakes every single beginner makes, myself included, back in the day.")
th("One. Overloading the fragrance. More oil does not mean more scent. Past a certain point it just refuses to bind and ruins the burn. Stay in the safe range.")
br("An amber fragrance bottle being measured carefully on a small kitchen scale.","sets an amber fragrance bottle on a small kitchen scale and measures the fragrance carefully")
th("Two. Pouring too hot. Hot wax into a cold jar gives you wet spots and sinkholes. Let it cool into the proper window before it ever touches the glass.")
th("Three. Rushing the cooling. Shoving a candle in the fridge to set it faster wrecks the top every time. Slow and undisturbed always wins.")
th("Avoid those three, measure your temperatures, and your first real candle will be better than most people's tenth. I promise you that.")
