br("The five genuinely useful tools laid out together: a pouring pot, thermometer, scale, stirrer, and wick holder.","lays out a pouring pot, a thermometer, a small scale, a stirrer and a wick holder together in a neat group")
th("The scale matters more than people expect, because good candle making is done by weight, not by volume. You weigh your wax and you weigh your fragrance.")
th("Weighing is what makes a candle repeatable. A recipe in grams can be made the exact same way a hundred times. A recipe in cups never can.")
th("Everything beyond that little list, the fancy melters, the heat guns, the molds, can wait until you actually know you need them. Do not let gear become the hobby.")
th("I made beautiful candles for a year with a pot, a thermometer, a scale and a spoon. The tools did not make the candle. The temperatures did.")
